2b9.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x) \\Rightarrow P(x).$ $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\n- Option III reads\n![](images/1f/1f472c122fe745e97fb31328625eccb71515dfee4b99e4bba548bf367cc8cc78.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $P(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x).$ $\\:{\\color{darkgreen}\\checkmark}$\n\n- Option IV reads\n![](images/52/525a046232143aa333ded66fb2bec55ff0011a8f76ef74373b9c6c99abdc3fd3.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x) \\Rightarrow P(x).$ $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198283 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c2b5afd8-4be0-5217-be25-bcd0b5c0bdf4" "question-03f10976-674d-5f7f-9c6a-ec5de8c4e5cb" "question-e85c3130-f931-5905-869c-d8f851fcf1f1"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198187 :question/problem "Complete the following table:\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| $B$ is sufficient for $A$ |  |\n| For $A,$ it is sufficient that $B$ |  |\n| $B$ is necessary for $A$ |  |\n| For $A,$ it is necessary that $B$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S \\Rightarrow N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\textbf{S}\\textrm{ufficient} \\: \\Rightarrow \\: \\textbf{N}\\textrm{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S\\Rightarrow N{:}$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"$B$ is sufficient for $A$\" means $B\\Rightarrow A.$\n\n- \"For $A,$ it is sufficient that $B$\" means $B\\Rightarrow A.$\n\n- \"$B$ is necessary for $A$\" means $A\\Rightarrow B.$\n\n- \"For $A,$ it is necessary that $B$\" means $A\\Rightarrow B.$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| $B$ is sufficient for $A$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}B\\Rightarrow A}$ |\n| For $A,$ it is sufficient that $B$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}B\\Rightarrow A}$ |\n| $B$ is necessary for $A$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}A\\Rightarrow B}$ |\n| For $A,$ it is necessary that $B$ | $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}A\\Rightarrow B}$ |" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198284 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7bd7ef2d-fe07-5622-9cee-22e524115939" "question-6c169f1d-e661-56e4-b29a-c746d6d144a3" "question-78f9226d-96f1-55af-96d5-28d4a76505e9" "question-50849cc0-0b42-5b52-abb5-e0bdf56880ef"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198188 :question/problem "Consider the following predicates:\n\n$\\qquad$ $P(x):$ $x\\in\\mathbb {Z}^{-}$ $\\qquad$ $Q(x):$ $x$ is negative\n\nWhich of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x)?$\n\n- Whenever $x$ is negative, then $x\\in\\mathbb {Z}^{-}$\n\n- $x$ is negative whenever $x\\in\\mathbb {Z}^{-}$\n\n- $x$ is negative, provided that $x\\in\\mathbb {Z}^{-}$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $P \\Rightarrow Q$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n![](images/21/21fd3acc1e0a8862b0010d28252278e204bfe6c25abb66aed01f31cc0a565642.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x) \\Rightarrow P(x).$ $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\n- Option II reads\n![](images/44/4436567914aa607eae98ac50a467d6d6be1715d7b1f9cdfa0f907dc0df8b99ba.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $P(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x).$ $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\n- Option III reads\n![](images/30/305d426cb7c241d68ab4576848ae519429b58e3ae655cb65c23dc74c09d0722e.svg)\nwhich corresponds to $P(x) \\Rightarrow Q(x).$ $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198285 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f00a0a1e-c589-5b06-8786-738dfcf01ab1" "question-4c8d7440-4eac-56af-a31b-85c3ab92c898" "question-204c3d5d-7433-5e9d-bacd-9011685dc6a9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198185 :question/problem "Express $P \\Leftrightarrow Q$ as a sentence given the following:\n\n- $P:$ $A \\cup B = A.$\n\n- $Q:$ $B \\subseteq A.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P\\Leftrightarrow Q{:}$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nTherefore, some correct grammatical constructions of $P \\Leftrightarrow Q$ are the following:\n\n- $A \\cup B = A$ **if and only if** $B \\subseteq A.$\n\n- $A \\cup B = A$ **iff** $B \\subseteq A.$\n\n- $A \\cup B = A$ **is necessary and sufficient for** $B \\subseteq A.$\n\n- $A \\cup B = A$ **is equivalent to** $B \\subseteq A.$\n\n- **If** $A \\cup B = A,$ **then** $B \\subseteq A,$ **and conversely**." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-9945bf92-98ba-5f75-97ed-5d58f6f2c509" :question/id #uuid "9945bf92-98ba-5f75-97ed-5d58f6f2c509" :question/math-academy-id "q-183425" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following table:\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| {{field-1}} | $B⇒A$ |\n| {{field-2}} | $A⇒B$ |\n| {{field-3}} | $A⇒B$ |\n| {{field-4}} | $B⇒A$ |" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- If $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $P$ only if $Q$\n\n- $Q$ if $P$\n\n- $P$ implies $Q$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"If $B,$ then $A$\" means $B⇒A$\n\n- \"$A$ only if $B$\" means $A⇒B$\n\n- \"$B$ if $A$\" means $A⇒B$\n\n- \"$B$ implies $A$\" means $B⇒A$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| If $B,$ then $A$ | $B⇒A$ |\n| $A$ only if $B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $B$ if $A$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $B$ implies $A$ | $B⇒A$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a5796e8c-4ce3-5027-a97a-54e9d10f7fa5" "answer-field-4186b453-dd49-5cc7-a178-1d60b7b096f4" "answer-field-3c4e23a4-1fec-5702-9d2e-357515bd4eaf" "answer-field-ed29bf98-6439-5f8d-ba13-67776fb01e60"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a5796e8c-4ce3-5027-a97a-54e9d10f7fa5" :answer-field/id #uuid "a5796e8c-4ce3-5027-a97a-54e9d10f7fa5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-fe4ca48a-c26f-5767-b8f7-284b3e0fa724" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ae704d1f-c0d6-5573-b476-c1d71d095523" "answer-fe4ca48a-c26f-5767-b8f7-284b3e0fa724"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae704d1f-c0d6-5573-b476-c1d71d095523" :answer/id #uuid "ae704d1f-c0d6-5573-b476-c1d71d095523" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "If $A,$ then $B$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fe4ca48a-c26f-5767-b8f7-284b3e0fa724" :answer/id #uuid "fe4ca48a-c26f-5767-b8f7-284b3e0fa724" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "If $B,$ then $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4186b453-dd49-5cc7-a178-1d60b7b096f4" :answer-field/id #uuid "4186b453-dd49-5cc7-a178-1d60b7b096f4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-799e7f78-8dac-5ad2-99e7-33d91db9ab00" :answer-field/choices ["answer-799e7f78-8dac-5ad2-99e7-33d91db9ab00" "answer-c8e7c202-fc22-573c-80e3-4cc364ca4331"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-799e7f78-8dac-5ad2-99e7-33d91db9ab00" :answer/id #uuid "799e7f78-8dac-5ad2-99e7-33d91db9ab00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only if $B$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c8e7c202-fc22-573c-80e3-4cc364ca4331" :answer/id #uuid "c8e7c202-fc22-573c-80e3-4cc364ca4331" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answe