nt that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"$B$ is sufficient for $A$\" means $B⇒A.$\n\n- \"For $A,$ it is sufficient that $B$\" means $B⇒A.$\n\n- \"$B$ is necessary for $A$\" means $A⇒B.$\n\n- \"For $B,$ it is necessary that $A$\" means $B⇒A.$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| $B\\text{ is sufficient for }A$ | $B⇒A$ |\n| $\\text{For }A,\\text{ it is sufficient that }B$ | $B⇒A$ |\n| $B\\text{ is necessary for }A$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $\\text{For }B,\\text{ it is necessary that }A$ | $B⇒A$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186196284 :answer-field/correct 17592186196286 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186196287 :answer-field/correct "answer-c6446251-0a1d-57ac-8c2a-b02bffac4fa6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c6446251-0a1d-57ac-8c2a-b02bffac4fa6" "answer-d89b0608-c051-5f16-b024-17a6fd5fd14e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6446251-0a1d-57ac-8c2a-b02bffac4fa6" :answer/id #uuid "c6446251-0a1d-57ac-8c2a-b02bffac4fa6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "For $A,$ it is sufficient that $B$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d89b0608-c051-5f16-b024-17a6fd5fd14e" :answer/id #uuid "d89b0608-c051-5f16-b024-17a6fd5fd14e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "For $B,$ it is sufficient that $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186196281 :answer-field/correct 17592186196282 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186196278 :answer-field/correct "answer-82d9ed58-92df-51b0-8f6a-20e5f0f9c9c5" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60e0be5d-31e1-5e6c-9b9d-7be47926bca6" "answer-82d9ed58-92df-51b0-8f6a-20e5f0f9c9c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60e0be5d-31e1-5e6c-9b9d-7be47926bca6" :answer/id #uuid "60e0be5d-31e1-5e6c-9b9d-7be47926bca6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "For $A,$ it is necessary that $B$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-82d9ed58-92df-51b0-8f6a-20e5f0f9c9c5" :answer/id #uuid "82d9ed58-92df-51b0-8f6a-20e5f0f9c9c5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "For $B,$ it is necessary that $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-03f10976-674d-5f7f-9c6a-ec5de8c4e5cb" :question/id #uuid "03f10976-674d-5f7f-9c6a-ec5de8c4e5cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-183510" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=-1$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\n- $x=-1$ is sufficient for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n- $x=-1$ is necessary for $(x-1)(x+1)=0$\n- For $(x-1)(x+1)=0,$ it is necessary that $x=-1$\n- For $x=-1,$ it is sufficient that $(x-1)(x+1)=0$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S⇒N:$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is sufficient for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is necessary for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0,}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{it is necessary that}\\,{{x=-1}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{x=-1,}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{it is sufficient that}\\,{{(x-1)(x+1)=0}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f88db5da-74c7-5a6c-8f64-068574198241"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f88db5da-74c7-5a6c-8f64-068574198241" :answer-field/id #uuid "f88db5da-74c7-5a6c-8f64-068574198241" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fb5963c4-6280-5a68-adcd-4bcc40dceab0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fb5963c4-6280-5a68-adcd-4bcc40dceab0" "answer-a92c8a27-c90f-55ba-900b-012f540a5175" "answer-ac43712d-08c1-5314-bc53-7add8e989850" "answer-0ef0d8fa-6fbc-553b-b26f-6d47fc529632" "answer-b2a82ac1-260b-5de1-9737-cad96665d7a8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb5963c4-6280-5a68-adcd-4bcc40dceab0" :answer/id #uuid "fb5963c4-6280-5a68-adcd-4bcc40dceab0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a92c8a27-c90f-55ba-900b-012f540a5175" :answer/id #uuid "a92c8a27-c90f-55ba-900b-012f540a5175" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, III and IV" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac43712d-08c1-5314-bc53-7add8e989850" :answer/id #uuid "ac43712d-08c1-5314-bc53-7add8e989850" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, III and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0ef0d8fa-6fbc-553b-b26f-6d47fc529632" :answer/id #uuid "0ef0d8fa-6fbc-553b-b26f-6d47fc529632" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b2a82ac1-260b-5de1-9737-cad96665d7a8" :answer/id #uuid "b2a82ac1-260b-5de1-9737-cad96665d7a8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e85c3130-f931-5905-869c-d8f851fcf1f1" :question/id #uuid "e85c3130-f931-5905-869c-d8f851fcf1f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-183494" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following table:\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| {{field-1}} | $A⇒B$ |\n| {{field-2}} | $A⇒B$ |\n| {{field-3}} | $B⇒A$ |\n| {{field-4}} | $B⇒A$ |" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S⇒N:$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"$A$ is sufficient for $B$\" means $A⇒B.$\n\n- \"For $B,$ it is sufficient that $A$\" means $A⇒B.$\n\n- \"$A$ is necessary for $B$\" means $B⇒A.$\n\n- \"For $B,$ it is necessary that $A$\" means $B⇒A.$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| $A\\text{ is sufficient for }B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $\\text{For }B,\\text{ it is sufficient that }A$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $A\\text{ is necessary for }B$ | $B⇒A$ |\n| $\\text{For }B,\\text{ it is necessary that }A$ | $B⇒A$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d2826f1b-a2e2-59b1-8c2c-305d06b41a33" "answer-field-78a11872-cceb-5293-8402-caf231a9b11d" "answer-field-c308fe39-1766-5862-849d-a1cc5b467d23" "answer-field-fda8fd4f-bed5-5358-9090-1f5b69f10176"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d2826f1b-a2e2-59b1-8c2c-305d06b41a33" :answer-field/id #uuid "d2826f1b-a2e2-59b1-8c2c-305d06b41a33" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-dd1d205d-afcb-5d3d-94d6-0371c4c9c3f0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-dd1d205d-afcb-5d3d-94d6-0371c4c9c3f0" "answer-3ee7818c-a522-5908-9995-35d90101626c"] :db/ensure [:answe