id #uuid "2d340cc1-7ae4-5ed1-b834-2bf7786058f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ is necessary for $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fda8fd4f-bed5-5358-9090-1f5b69f10176" :answer-field/id #uuid "fda8fd4f-bed5-5358-9090-1f5b69f10176" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-9c5ac6d9-131f-5e46-9019-7fb72a6b2f5b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9e69bfe5-73c7-5471-89e3-e9d63c7f7dc3" "answer-9c5ac6d9-131f-5e46-9019-7fb72a6b2f5b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e69bfe5-73c7-5471-89e3-e9d63c7f7dc3" :answer/id #uuid "9e69bfe5-73c7-5471-89e3-e9d63c7f7dc3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "For $A,$ it is necessary that $B$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9c5ac6d9-131f-5e46-9019-7fb72a6b2f5b" :answer/id #uuid "9c5ac6d9-131f-5e46-9019-7fb72a6b2f5b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "For $B,$ it is necessary that $A$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186198859 :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $6\\,|\\,x$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $3\\,|\\,x$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\n- $6\\,|\\,x$ is sufficient for $3\\,|\\,x$\n- For $3\\,|\\,x,$ it is sufficient that $6\\,|\\,x$\n- $6\\,|\\,x$ is necessary for $3\\,|\\,x$\n- For $6\\,|\\,x,$ it is necessary that $3\\,|\\,x$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $S⇒N$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- $S$ is a *sufficient condition* for $N.$\n\n- $N$ is a *necessary condition* for $S.$\n\nThese ideas can be summarized as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{S}\\text{ufficient}\\,⇒\\,\\text{N}\\text{ecessary}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nWe have the following grammatical constructions for $S⇒N:$\n\n- $S$ is sufficient for $N$\n\n- For $N,$ it is sufficient that $S$\n\n- $N$ is necessary for $S$\n\n- For $S,$ it is necessary that $N$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n{{6\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is sufficient for}\\,{{3\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{3\\,|\\,x,}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{it is sufficient that}\\,{{6\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{6\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{is necessary for}\\,{{3\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n\\text{for}\\,{{6\\,|\\,x,}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{it is necessary that}\\,{{3\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and IV only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186196290 :answer-field/correct 17592186196293 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-7bd7ef2d-fe07-5622-9cee-22e524115939" :question/id #uuid "7bd7ef2d-fe07-5622-9cee-22e524115939" :question/math-academy-id "q-183566" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $x=0$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ ${x}^{2}=x$\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\n- Whenever $x=0,$ then ${x}^{2}=x$\n- ${x}^{2}=x$ whenever $x=0$\n- $x=0,$ provided that ${x}^{2}=x$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $P⇒Q$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\text{Whenever}\\,{{x=0\\text{,}}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{then}\\,{{{x}^{2}=x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{{x}^{2}=x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{whenever}\\,{{x=0}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{x=0\\text{,}}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{provided that}\\,{{{x}^{2}=x}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cb5ffcf8-bc22-542f-9944-294204fb67c6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cb5ffcf8-bc22-542f-9944-294204fb67c6" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb5ffcf8-bc22-542f-9944-294204fb67c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9d633d9a-da33-5e88-94db-67f637b7f7e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9d633d9a-da33-5e88-94db-67f637b7f7e2" "answer-9bdb2a41-ea7b-512e-8918-cc67d1d238e1" "answer-0a8ce566-6890-582f-a158-b42ec0895248" "answer-6d1c3f5e-ef37-5163-947d-6521fd9e875a" "answer-fde546f5-de83-5d7c-8c8e-c9d84f7e0b85"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9d633d9a-da33-5e88-94db-67f637b7f7e2" :answer/id #uuid "9d633d9a-da33-5e88-94db-67f637b7f7e2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I  and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9bdb2a41-ea7b-512e-8918-cc67d1d238e1" :answer/id #uuid "9bdb2a41-ea7b-512e-8918-cc67d1d238e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I  and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a8ce566-6890-582f-a158-b42ec0895248" :answer/id #uuid "0a8ce566-6890-582f-a158-b42ec0895248" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6d1c3f5e-ef37-5163-947d-6521fd9e875a" :answer/id #uuid "6d1c3f5e-ef37-5163-947d-6521fd9e875a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II  and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fde546f5-de83-5d7c-8c8e-c9d84f7e0b85" :answer/id #uuid "fde546f5-de83-5d7c-8c8e-c9d84f7e0b85" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6c169f1d-e661-56e4-b29a-c746d6d144a3" :question/id #uuid "6c169f1d-e661-56e4-b29a-c746d6d144a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-183527" :question/problem "Find the missing entries in the following table:\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| Whenever $A,$ then $B$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $A$ whenever $B$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $A,$ provided that $B$ | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nLet's now compare these against the entries in our table:\n\n- \"Whenever $A,$ then $B$\" means $A⇒B$\n\n- \"$A$ whenever $B$\" means $B⇒A$\n\n- \"$A,$ provided that $B$\" means $B⇒A$\n\nThe completed table is shown below.\n\n| Sentence | Symbolic Form |\n| --- | --- |\n| Whenever $A,$ then $B$ | $A⇒B$ |\n| $A$ whenever $B$ | $B⇒A$ |\n| $A,$ provided that $B$ | $B⇒A$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e38ec42d-bc75-5c8d-9cc7-a3f9b8be8339" "answer-field-eb4cd898-fb85-5c29-b484-558ddab6c1a3" "answer-field-dc6f13fe-2a99-5d7e-ae68-45d38a11565e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e38ec42d-bc75-5c8d-9cc7-a3f9b8be8339" :answer-field/id #uuid "e38ec42d-bc75-5c8d-9cc7-a3f9b8be8339" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-b46318ad-fba0-55d4-96a7-2a0d90f45007" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b46318ad-fba0-55d4-96a7-2a0d90f45007" "answer-2a72e058-271b-5aa6-80fa-533e0bbc2a15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b46318ad-fba0-55d4-96a7-2a0d90f45007" :answer/id #uuid "b46318ad-fba0-55d4-96a7-2a0d90f45007" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a72e058-271b-5aa6-80fa-533e0bbc2a15" :answer/id #uuid "2a72e058-271b-5aa6-80fa-533e0bbc2a15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B⇒A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eb4cd898-fb85-5c29-b484-558ddab6c1a3" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb4cd898-fb85-5c29-b484-558ddab6c1a3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-efd25ca7-6e00-5e96-838d-79c52832e8fc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aaa6189c-399e-5a74-b48d-faee10d7afe4" "answer-efd25ca7-6e00-5e96-838d-79c52832e8fc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aaa6189c-399e-5a74-b48d-faee10d7afe4" :answer/id #uuid "aaa6189c-399e-5a74-b48d-faee10d7afe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efd25ca7-6e00-5e96-838d-79c52832e8fc" :answer/id #uuid "efd25ca7-6e00-5e96-838d-79c52832e8fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B⇒A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dc6f13fe-2a99-5d7e-ae68-45d38a11565e" :answer-field/id #uuid "dc6f13fe-2a99-5d7e-ae68-45d38a11565e" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-1bdadf87-28de-5f43-b22e-91359b75ecaf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0d6844ae-27ea-5374-a438-c24d7e669095" "answer-1bdadf87-28de-5f43-b22e-91359b75ecaf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d6844ae-27ea-5374-a438-c24d7e669095" :answer/id #uuid "0d6844ae-27ea-5374-a438-c24d7e669095" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "A⇒B" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1bdadf87-28de-5f43-b22e-91359b75ecaf" :answer/id #uuid "1bdadf87-28de-5f43-b22e-91359b75ecaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "B⇒A" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-78f9226d-96f1-55af-96d5-28d4a76505e9" :question/id #uuid "78f9226d-96f1-55af-96d5-28d4a76505e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-183533" :question/problem "$\\,$ $P(x):$ $4\\,|\\,x$ $\\,$ $Q(x):$ $x$ is composite\n\nConsider the predicates $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ above. Which of the following expresses the conditional predicate $P(x)⇒Q(x)?$\n\n- Whenever $4\\,|\\,x,$ then $x$ is composite\n- $4\\,|\\,x$ whenever $x$ is composite\n- $x$ is composite, provided that $4\\,|\\,x$" :question/worked-solution "Given that the implication $P⇒Q$ is true, we have the following:\n\n- Whenever $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $Q$ whenever $P$\n\n- $Q,$ provided that $P$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\text{Whenever}\\,{{4\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)},\\,\\text{then}\\,{{x\\text{ is composite}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{4\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{whenever}\\,{{x\\text{ is composite}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\text{ is composite,}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{provided that}\\,{{4\\,|\\,x}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b060c187-cb85-5841-a5af-47c6d7c784ad"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b060c187-cb85-5841-a5af-47c6d7c784ad" :answer-field/id #uuid "b060c187-cb85-5841-a5af-47c6d7c784ad" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-320b80df-22ed-5e98-ad73-2f1d0474fa78" :answer-field/choices ["answer-41f5ede5-5a8e-58dc-84d4-9753affb83f0" "answer-320b80df-22ed-5e98-ad73-2f1d0474fa78" "answer-addc3e96-7972-50b2-ae08-63e88d8f6e78" "answer-9df674b4-222e-5226-8472-65f74b544b1a" "answer-59e660dd-80d7-5d3d-9256-060d4013846a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-41f5ede5-5a8e-58dc-84d4-9753affb83f0" :answer/id #uuid "41f5ede5-5a8e-58dc-84d4-9753affb83f0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-320b80df-22ed-5e98-ad73-2f1d0474fa78" :answer/id #uuid "320b80df-22ed-5e98-ad73-2f1d0474fa78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-addc3e96-7972-50b2-ae08-63e88d8f6e78" :answer/id #uuid "addc3e96-7972-50b2-ae08-63e88d8f6e78" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/va